Obama’s first and most important job is to protect our families and children – and that includes our schools. In 2012, when the Sandy Hook massacre took place, I wrote to the president. I said:

“As a father of two school-aged children and a grandfather of two school-aged children, I am deeply concerned about the safety of our schools, and I believe that you have a responsibility to take steps to protect our schoolchildren. I have seen the results of school shootings and other violent acts in other countries. I have seen the results of gun violence in my own community. I have seen the results of inaction. The people of Newtown, CT, and across the country have been waiting for you to act. They are waiting to hear from you that you will take action to protect our schools.”

Today, I am renewing my call for President Obama to take action to keep our schools safe. I am urging Congress to pass a law that will:

· Require background checks on all gun purchases;

· Require guns to be stored safely away from children;

· Require gun owners to report lost or stolen firearms to law enforcement;

